title: Cross-machine sync
tags: Sync
kind: reference
status: deferred
summary: Syncing with a repository on another machine is not built: both repositories must be loaded in one daemon, and a store may not live on a network filesystem.

Every sync primitive needs both repositories loaded in the same daemon
([[Sync endpoints]]), and a repository's store is refused on a network filesystem
([[Storage safety]]): mounting a remote repository over SSHFS and loading it is not
an option.

The way proposed (September 2026) is to bring the remote repository's store over for
the sync:

# copy the remote `.metafolder/` to the local disk, as an external `.metafolder` whose root is the mount of the remote files — its roots rewritten, its store copied consistently (`mf repo backup`);
# sync against that local copy, as against any loaded repository;
# send the synced `.metafolder/` back, replacing the remote one.

Nothing may write to the remote repository in between, or step 3 loses it: the copy
would hold a lock on the remote — a marker its daemon refuses to load past, lifted by
step 3. Neither the commands nor that lock exist.
